zlib is copyright Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler, under the zlib license.
The complete upstream notice is retained in LICENSE and the public zlib.h.
The exact release archive and checksum are recorded in share/zlib/source.txt.

Pyxis builds unmodified upstream sources as a static core library, including
compression/decompression, checksums and compress/uncompress convenience APIs.
The default allocators and shipped static tables are retained. The build omits
gz file I/O, contrib, shared libraries and upstream programs/tests.

The public zlib.h and zconf.h remain unmodified. They also declare gz file APIs
that this profile does not provide; those APIs are unavailable at link time.
No host libc, source patches or compatibility stubs are included.
